et. **Considered-but-declined-with-a-reason is a third category between used and ignored, and it is the one that shows discrimination rather than mere matching.**", :metric-2-memories-saved 0, :now-unblocked {:headline "**a94J04's poissonConv_L2_contraction IS NOW A DIRECT APPLICATION OF AN IMPORTABLE, AXIOM-CLEAN THEOREM. THE ROW SHOULD BE RE-DISPATCHED, NOT LEFT BLOCKED.**", :verification "I checked rather than inferred. `import YoungL2` now resolves and `#print axioms convolution_L2_contraction_of_probability_kernel` gives [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. Its signature is: for g f : R -> R, (forall x, 0 <= g x) -> (int g = 1) -> MemLp f 2 volume -> eLpNorm (fun x => int g (x - y) * f y) 2 volume <= eLpNorm f 2 volume.", :hypotheses-already-proved "**THIS RUN PROVED THE EXACT HYPOTHESES THE THEOREM NEEDS**: poissonKernel_integral_one gives int g = 1, and Poisson-kernel nonnegativity is immediate. The runner proved the inputs to a theorem it could not reach.", :caveat "poissonConv_tendsto_L2 and poissonConv_tendsto_ae are NOT unblocked by this. The runner states tendsto_L2 additionally needs the integral-valued approximate-identity estimate combining the contraction with Continuous.compMeasurePreservingLp. Only the contraction target is newly reachable -- do not overstate this to three targets.", :recommended-action "Re-dispatch a94J04 targeting poissonConv_L2_contraction, with the packet naming `import YoungL2` and `convolution_L2_contraction_of_probability_kernel` (root namespace, NOT YoungL2.convolution_... -- I checked, the qualified path does not resolve)."}, :metric-3-memories-used 2, :sorry-delta-scoping "File count 6 -> 3; DISPATCHED-TARGET count 4 -> 1. Both reported because they differ and the row was dispatched on the target subset.", :classification :partial-now-unblocked-by-infrastructure-fix, :axioms-verified-independently true, :receipt-lateness "Recorded late: the result completed hours before this receipt and the row sat :status :dispatched with :receipt nil. Third and last of the stale-dispatched rows to be cleared.", :metric-1-problems-solved 0, :axiom-verification "re-elaborated from a /tmp scratch copy, not trusting the runner: all four ApmCanaries.A94J04 declarations [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. Exactly 3 executable sorries remain (lines 207, 225, 241). lake env lean exit 0.", :result :axiom-clean-partial, :natural-experiment {:headline "**THIS RUN IS THE CONTROL ARM OF AN ACCIDENTAL BEFORE/AFTER EXPERIMENT ON THE MODULE-PATH DEFECT, AND IT IS THE CLEANEST EVIDENCE OF THAT DEFECT'S COST.**", :what-the-runner-hit "Its error log records: `YoungL2 was an unknown module prefix: the root-level proved file is not part of any Lake library, so it was not imported as if available.` Its stated exact obstruction: `YoungL2.lean contains an axiom-clean convolution_L2_contraction_of_probability_kernel, but it is outside all configured Lake libraries and therefore cannot be imported reproducibly.`", :timeline "**a94J04 dispatched 03:40:08. I committed the lakefile fix 7958c53 at 03:52:44 -- twelve minutes later, prompted by this very report. a96A04 dispatched 05:00:57 and its runner reported `The repository's YoungL2 module closed heatConv_L2_le`.** Same repository, same module, same theorem: blocked before the fix, discharged a declaration after it.", :why-it-matters "Infrastructure defects in this corpus are usually argued from first principles. Here the cost and the repair are both directly observed, 80 minutes apart, with no other variable changed."}, :commit "1078e8b2039793848826d6951949e63e739ec5ac", :sorry-delta-headline -3, :metric-3-memories-surfaced 5, :declarations-newly-usable ["poissonKernel_integral_one" "poissonKernel_integrable" "poissonKernel_integral_Ioo" "poissonKernel_tail_tendsto"], :sorry-delta-genuine-discharges -3, :search-audit "arm (a) carried all completed work and named its components precisely (integral_univ_inv_one_add_sq, integral_div_sq_add_sq, Measure.integral_comp_div, integral_add_compl, Real.tendsto_arctan_atTop). Arms (b) and (c) deliberately not attempted because the route was known -- stated as such rather than reported as empty.", :detail "a94J04 partial. Four declarations closed axiom-clean; dispatched-target sorries 4 -> 1. Its blocking report caused the lakefile fix that unblocked it, which is now verified reachable."}, :runner "codex-7", :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:codex-pilot :partial :module-path-defect :natural-experiment :younglib-payoff :now-unblocked :memory-use :late-receipt], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:46:42.048152554Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :problem, :ref/id "a94J04"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "edacc884-c0d1-4832-9303-83a737c2ed73"} {:evidence/body {:job-id "invoke-1785459812871-423-96015ad9", :phase :outcome, :problem "a02J03", :row-kind :hard-proof-step, :runner-model :codex, :outcome {:vacuity-check-run "0a/0b clean across all five declarations: no True conclusions, the sole definition scaledIntOp is genuine (not a bare constant), no inline (h : True) binders.", :recall-outcome-verbatim "[dispatch-recall-outcome=timeout]", :metric-2-memories-saved 0, :metric-3-memories-used :NOT-MEASURABLE, :metric-3-note "Recorded :NOT-MEASURABLE, not 0. **The runner itself declined the inference**, writing `this is infrastructure unavailability and no inference about memory coverage was made` -- the typed recall banner working as designed for the fourth time tonight. Cause now diagnosed: evidence/text-search costs ~9-16s per subject against a 30s TOTAL recall budget (receipt 4f7eeadd-3072-41ab-94f2-effe22e62ae0).", :route "linear change of variables for Lebesgue integration: rewrote the interval indicator under x |-> kx, applied Measure.integral_comp_mul_left, used hphi on [ka,kb], normalized the rational expression.", :classification :partial-with-two-statements-false, :statement-defect-found {:mechanism :integral-undef-totalisation, :diagnosis-status :argued-not-machine-checked, :proposed-repair "Add `LocallyIntegrable phi volume` (or an equivalent local-integrability / measurability hypothesis). Under it, differentiation gives the required essential bound and the intended L1-density argument becomes valid.", :diagnosis-status-note "ARGUED. The construction is standard and fully specified, but neither counterexample was formalised in Lean. Recorded explicitly because this lane has conflated argued with proved before.", :uniform-bound-refutation "Choose a finite positive-measure F on which psi is bounded and bounded away from zero; set f = indicator F, k = 1, phi = C*psi. Then f and phi*f are integrable, and taking C large makes |int phi*f| > M * int ||f||, while every interval hypothesis still reads 0 <= ... .", :counterexample-construction "**The runner supplied an explicit witness rather than an impossibility argument, which is what makes this a refutation and not a difficulty report.** There exist nonnegative measurable, finite-a.e. psi : R -> R that are non-integrable on EVERY nonempty interval -- enumerate rational intervals repeatedly, place increasingly tall spikes on sets of summable measure, and use Borel-Cantelli to keep pointwise finiteness while every interval integral diverges. Mathlib's `integral_undef` then gives int_{Icc a b} psi = 0 for every a < b, so the hypothesis hphi holds VACUOUSLY for any positive M.", :taxonomy "**THIS IS THE UMBRELLA MECHANISM AGAIN -- `missing semantic-domain guards admit degenerate witnesses`, integral_undef branch.** Prior instances: a01A10, a01J01, a02J01, a95A08. This makes at least a fifth, and the umbrella keeps predicting rather than merely describing.", :decision-owner "joe", :verdict :BOTH-FALSE-AS-STATED, :declarations ["uniform_bound" "scaled_integral_vanishes"], :scaled-integral-refutation "Set phi = 1 + psi. A diagonal weighting produces a positive integrable f with every (1 + psi(n.))f integrable, and along positive integers scaledIntOp phi f n >= int f > 0. So the scaled integrals do not tend to zero, though every interval integral in hphi is zero."}, :axioms-verified-independently true, :receipt-lateness "**Recorded late.** This result completed hours before the receipt was written; the row sat :status :dispatched with :receipt nil, and it surfaced only during an audit of stale dispatched rows. Reading a result is not processing it. Three rows were in this state; this is the second cleared.", :metric-1-problems-solved 0, :axiom-verification "re-elaborated from a /tmp scratch copy, not trusting the runner: indicator_bound [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. Exactly 2 executable sorries remain (lines 113, 133). lake env lean exit 0.", :result :axiom-clean-partial, :commit "591bbedb67cbbe6fb36920599e0096fdeda0643e", :sorry-delta-headline -1, :metric-3-memories-surfaced :NOT-MEASURABLE, :declarations-newly-usable ["indicator_bound"], :sorry-delta-genuine-discharges -1, :search-audit "arm (a) carried the completed proof and named its components (Measure.integral_comp_mul_left, MeasureTheory.integral_indicator, Set.indicator_of_mem/notMem). Arm (b) Zulip returned no anchor. Arm (c) arXiv deliberately not attempted -- appropriate, since the remaining obstruction is an explicit counterexample mechanism, not a literature gap, and the runner said so rather than reporting an arm it had not run.", :detail "a02J03 partial. One declaration closed axiom-clean; the other two targets are FALSE as stated, refuted by an explicit integral_undef witness rather than merely unproved."}, :runner "codex-6", :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:codex-pilot :partial :statement-false :integral-undef :umbrella-mechanism :recall-timeout :late-receipt], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:44:43.940884560Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :problem, :ref/id "a02J03"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "80f484cb-d5cd-49fb-bb23-20d9a1212344"} {:evidence/body {:phase :infrastructure-diagnosis, :outcome {:headline "**THE metric-3 TIMEOUTS ARE NOT STORE PRESSURE. THE RECALL BUDGET IS SMALLER THAN THE COST OF THE QUERIES RECALL MUST MAKE.**", :conclusion "**RECALL CANNOT COMPLETE FOR ANY ROW WITH MORE THAN ABOUT TWO COMMON SUBJECT TERMS, ON A HEALTHY STORE.** That is a structural mismatch between default-recall-timeout-ms (30000) and the cost of evidence/text-search (~9-16s each, 6-12 calls). It is not transient and no restart fixes it.", :but-thresholds-not-met "**The restart trigger fired while its underlying condition was absent.** At that moment: host memory 15 GB available of 30 GB (threshold: < 4 GB); store JVM RSS 7.0 GB (threshold: > 10 GB); the evidence endpoint answering in 0.22s with http 200. Restarting on the trigger alone would have been cargo-cult, so I measured the recall path instead of restarting reflexively.", :consequence-for-the-metric "**metric-3 has been SYSTEMATICALLY UNDER-MEASURED, and the bias is not random**: it falls hardest on rows whose subjects are common mathematical vocabulary -- i.e. the analysis-heavy rows. Every `:NOT-MEASURABLE` I recorded tonight is honest, but the whitepaper should not read them as `recall found nothing`; it should read them as `recall was not given time to answer`. This does NOT retract any recorded memory USE (those are positive observations); it bounds the denominator.", :classification :recall-budget-structurally-too-small, :measurement {:method "Timed each seam the recall path actually calls (src/futon3c/dispatch_with_recall.clj): receipt-entries, memory/projection, and evidence/text-search -- one text-search PER SUBJECT, with subjects_for() yielding up to 12 per row.", :recall-budget-ms 30000, :budget-note "default-recall-timeout-ms = 30000 is the TOTAL budget; per-call-timeout-ms is max(250, recall-timeout-ms), so a single slow seam can consume the whole thing.", :receipt-entries "2.3s (200 rows, 16 entries) -- not the problem.", :text-search-before-restart "{\"deriv\" \"29.9s / 204KB\", \"zero\" \"32.1s / 185KB\", \"isopen\" \"16.5s / 459KB\", \"differentiableon\" \"13.5s\", \"count\" \"13.7s / 403KB\", \"roots\" \"13.3s\"}", :controlled-comparison "**Subject COUNT does not explain the timeouts.** construction-deriv timed out with 6 subjects; a97A08 COMPLETED with 6. What differs is per-term cost, which tracks how COMMON the term is in the corpus: construction-deriv's subjects are deriv/zero/isopen/differentiableon -- among the most frequent tokens in a Lean analysis corpus.", :totals-before "construction-deriv's 6 subjects: 92.1s total. a97A08's 6 subjects: 79.0s total. **BOTH exceed the 30s budget**, including the row that had succeeded earlier -- so the endpoint had degraded over the session."}, :trigger "Three of the last four dispatches recorded [dispatch-recall-outcome=timeout] (a97A07, a95J07, construction-deriv), two of them CONSECUTIVE -- which meets the documented restart threshold.", :restart-performed {:justification "Restarted on EVIDENCE of degradation (text-search at 30s+ per query), not on the trigger. Joe authorised store restarts this session.", :command "systemctl --user restart futon1b-server", :readiness "~75s to first 200 on the evidence endpoint.", :after "{\"deriv\" \"14.4s (was 29.9)\", \"zero\" \"16.0s (was 32.1)\", \"isopen\" \"9.1s (was 16.5)\", \"differentiableon\" \"14.6s (was 13.5)\", \"count\" \"16.2s (was 13.7)\", \"roots\" \"15.2s (was 13.3)\"}", :verdict "**The restart halved the degraded tail and confirmed accumulated state was part of it -- but it did NOT fix the problem.** The floor is ~9-16s per text-search query even on a fresh store. construction-deriv's six subjects would still cost ~86s against a 30s budget."}, :repair-options-not-applied {:cheapest "raise default-recall-timeout-ms from 30000 to ~120000 (one constant, src/futon3c/dispatch_with_recall.clj:19)", :next "cap or rank subjects_for() by rarity rather than taking the first 12 -- common tokens cost the most and discriminate least", :real-fix "index or paginate /api/alpha/evidence/text-search; returning 200-460KB per query is the underlying cost", :why-not-applied "**No dispatchable rows remain (queue drained), so nothing tonight depends on it, and changing recall timing changes dispatch behaviour for every future run.** A before/after measurement on a live dispatch is the right way to land it. Decision owner: joe."}}, :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:infrastructure :recall :metric-3 :measurement :budget-mis-specified :store-restart], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:42:38.070671915Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :infrastructure, :ref/id "dispatch-recall-budget"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :measurement, :evidence/id "4f7eeadd-3072-41ab-94f2-effe22e62ae0"} {:evidence/body {:job-id "invoke-1785471894052-473-80a5fb14", :phase :outcome, :problem "construction-deriv-ne-zero-of-injon", :row-kind :construction-target, :runner-model :codex, :outcome {:recall-outcome-verbatim "[dispatch-recall-outcome=timeout]", :metric-2-memories-saved 0, :metric-3-memories-used :NOT-MEASURABLE, :protocol-violation {:what "**I DISPATCHED THIS ROW IN ERROR. It carries `:do-not-redispatch true`** -- set because its frontier had been verified against Mathlib at chain-depth 3.", :how "My ad-hoc selection checked only a hardcoded three-id blocklist, and `codex_sorry_cron.choose_row` never consulted the flag either. The flag was further defeated by a state conflict I created: I had REOPENED the row to `:untouched` (its file still held an executable sorry), which made it selectable while the guard still said do-not.", :irreversible "There is no cancel endpoint on the Agency invoke API -- I tried POST .../cancel and DELETE; both 404. A mis-dispatch cannot be recalled.", :fix "Added `dispatch_blocked_reason(row)` to codex_sorry_cron.py, wired into choose_row; honours :do-not-redispatch and :depends-on-problem. Verified across all 88 rows (now blocks 6) and the 11 existing tests still pass."}, :and-yet {:headline "**THE MIS-DISPATCH PRODUCED REAL VALUE, AND THAT IS EVIDENCE THE GUARD WAS SET TOO EARLY -- NOT EVIDENCE THAT GUARDS ARE OPTIONAL.**", :detail "The row's recorded `:next-leaf` named TWO missing pieces: `local normal form` and `analytic k-th root`. **This run PROVED THE FIRST**: `exists_local_normal_form_of_deriv_eq_zero` gives `g w - g z = (w-z)^n * F w` locally with `2 <= n` and `F z != 0`, axiom-clean. It also added `analyticOrderAt_sub_self_ne_top_of_injOn`, excluding the infinite-order/eventually-constant case. The remaining obstruction is now strictly narrower: construct a local analytic n-th root of F/F(z), apply local open mapping, and pull back two values differing by a nontrivial n-th root of unity.", :frontier-rule-applied "**Under the sharpened rule -- count attempts that FAIL AT THE SAME POINT -- this did NOT fail at the same point.** The prior attempt stopped before the normal form; this one proved it and stopped one step later. That is a95A02's shape (assembly advancing piece by piece), not a95J08's (three attempts, one wall). **A `:do-not-redispatch` flag set on a frontier that is still ADVANCING is premature by exactly this test.**", :recommendation "Clear `:do-not-redispatch` on this row and re-mark it `:blocked-mathlib-frontier` with the NARROWED obstruction, so the next attempt starts from the normal form rather than re-deriving it. Decision owner: joe. **I am not clearing it myself** -- I violated this guard once tonight and will not also be the one to remove it.", :caveat "Honest counterweight: one advancing attempt does not prove the target is reachable. Mathlib genuinely lacks the assembly (the runner found cpow, open-mapping and root-of-unity components but no local-degree theorem), and I confirmed independently earlier tonight that Mathlib has no Rouche and no argument principle. The narrowing is real; the frontier is also real."}, :classification :partial-frontier-narrowed, :metric-1-problems-solved 0, :result :axiom-clean-partial, :commit "aac128093a745d143d26b6d917923f7f5b06ead1", :sorry-delta-headline 0, :metric-3-memories-surfaced :NOT-MEASURABLE, :declarations-newly-usable ["analyticOrderAt_sub_self_ne_top_of_injOn" "exists_local_normal_form_of_deriv_eq_zero"], :sorry-delta-genuine-discharges 0, :axioms-runner-reported "two_le_analyticOrderAt_sub_self, analyticOrderAt_sub_self_ne_top_of_injOn, exists_local_normal_form_of_deriv_eq_zero all [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; deriv_ne_zero_of_injOn still [propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. Sorry count 1 -> 1.", :detail "construction-deriv-ne-zero-of-injOn: mis-dispatched against its own guard, ran because there is no cancel path, and returned an axiom-clean narrowing partial that proved one of the two named missing pieces. Both facts recorded; neither cancels the other."}, :runner "codex-6", :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:codex-pilot :mis-dispatch :guard-violation :frontier-narrowed :do-not-redispatch-set-too-early :recall-timeout], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:42:06.491384874Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :construction-target, :ref/id "UnivalentDeriv"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "42e34d3b-7edb-4e61-98c7-f73f71f1178e"} {:evidence/body {:job-id "invoke-1785471544624-472-308f6c1d", :phase :outcome, :problem "a95J07", :row-kind :hard-proof-step, :runner-model :codex, :outcome {:recall-outcome-verbatim "[dispatch-recall-outcome=timeout]", :metric-2-memories-saved 0, :metric-3-memories-used :NOT-MEASURABLE, :metric-3-not-zero "Recorded :NOT-MEASURABLE, not 0. Second dispatch-recall timeout of the session (a97A07 was the first). **They were NOT consecutive** -- a97A08 completed-with-memories between them -- so the documented restart threshold (2 CONSECUTIVE recall failures) is not met and no store restart was performed. Recording the rate honestly: 2 timeouts in 6 dispatches this stretch.", :route "the 5r covering lemma. Mathlib's Zorn-based Vitali.exists_disjoint_subfamily_covering_enlargement supplied selection; Set.PairwiseDisjoint.countable_of_isOpen supplied countability; the family was then enumerated duplicate-free over N by injecting the subtype and padding unused indices with the empty set.", :classification :partial-with-statement-false, :statement-defect-found {:mechanism :missing-measurability-guard, :independent-check "**I CHECKED THE MATHEMATICS RATHER THAN ACCEPTING THE RUNNER'S CLAIM, AND IT IS DECISIVELY FALSE.** The classical Vitali construction partitions [0,1] into countably many pairwise disjoint translates each having OUTER measure 1. Their outer measures then sum to infinity, not to <= 1. So the statement is not merely unprovable -- an explicit countermodel exists in the standard literature.", :taxonomy-placement "**THIS BELONGS UNDER THE PASS-33 UMBRELLA -- `missing semantic-domain guards admit degenerate witnesses` -- as a FOURTH mechanism alongside integral_undef, totalized deriv, and extended-codomain top.** The shape is identical: an operation (`volume`) is TOTAL on all sets, silently degrading from measure to outer measure outside its intended domain, and the statement omits the guard that keeps it in that domain. It is not a placeholder defect and not API drift.", :diagnosis-status :argued-not-machine-checked, :proposed-repair "Add `(hS_meas : forall k, NullMeasurableSet (S k) volume)`, or require each S k to be an interval. NullMeasurableSet is the weaker and more natural of the two and suffices for countable additivity.", :diagnosis-status-note "ARGUED, not machine-checked: I did not formalise the Vitali counterexample in Lean. The argument is textbook and the countermodel is explicit, but the distinction is recorded because this lane has previously conflated argued with proved.", :decision-owner "joe", :verdict :FALSE-AS-STATED, :declaration "tsum_volume_disjoint_le_one", :detail "The statement assumes only that the S k are pairwise disjoint subsets of (0,1) and concludes sum_k volume (S k) <= 1. **Countable additivity requires measurability.** For non-measurable sets `volume` is the outer-measure extension, which is only countably SUBadditive, and disjointness buys nothing."}, :axioms-verified-independently true, :metric-1-problems-solved 0, :axiom-verification "re-elaborated from a /tmp scratch copy: vitali_covering_5 [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. One executable sorry remains (line 59). lake env lean exit 0.", :result :axiom-clean-partial, :commit "f7f0133790fbe4d40b826c0a1b00c3cc98e52864", :sorry-delta-headline -1, :metric-3-memories-surfaced :NOT-MEASURABLE, :declarations-newly-usable ["vitali_covering_5"], :sorry-delta-genuine-discharges -1, :search-audit "arm (a) carried the proof and named its Mathlib components precisely (Vitali.exists_disjoint_subfamily_covering_enlargement, Set.PairwiseDisjoint.countable_of_isOpen). Arms (b) and (c) were deliberately not attempted because the standard route and components were found directly -- an appropriate call, and the runner said so rather than reporting empty arms it had not run.", :detail "a95J07 partial. The HARDER target closed: vitali_covering_5, the 5r covering theorem, axiom-clean. The remaining helper is false as stated and needs a measurability hypothesis. Sorries 2 -> 1."}, :runner "codex-7", :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:codex-pilot :partial :statement-false :missing-measurability-guard :recall-timeout :metric-3-not-measurable], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:30:34.166933457Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :problem, :ref/id "a95J07"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "38d90cdc-7f89-452f-bed0-0117ee1dc07c"} {:evidence/body {:job-id "invoke-1785471377736-471-acbcd206", :phase :outcome, :problem "a97A08", :row-kind :hard-proof-step, :runner-model :codex, :outcome {:recall-outcome-verbatim "[dispatch-recall-outcome=completed-with-memories]", :metric-2-memories-saved 0, :metric-3-memories-used 1, :route "count_outer proved WITHOUT Rouche, by Cauchy's root bound: every root satisfies |z|^5 <= 15|z| + 1; if |z| >= 2 then |z|^5 >= 16|z| > 15|z| + 1, contradiction; algebraic closure plus degree five give exactly five roots. Neat -- the outer count needed no complex-analytic machinery at all.", :sorry-delta-note "**HEADLINE AND GENUINE DIFFER HERE AND THE RUNNER SAID SO ITSELF.** Sorries went 3 -> 1, but only ONE declaration became genuinely usable: apm_a97A08_count_outer. apm_a97A08_main's proof BODY was completed, which removed its lexical sorry, but it remains sorryAx-dependent through count_inner. This is consolidation, not discharge -- the exact distinction EXECUTABLE-SORRIES cannot make. **Credit to the runner: it disclosed this unprompted and printed the sorryAx axiom line rather than reporting a clean 3 -> 1.**", :leverage-finding {:headline "**ONE SORRY NOW BLOCKS THREE PROBLEMS: ConstructionTargets/Rouche.lean:102, zeroCountInClosedBall_add_eq.**", :detail "apm_a97A08_count_inner needs Rouche with dominant term 15X and perturbation X^5 + 1. **The boundary inequality is already proved**; what is missing is homotopy invariance of total divisor count -- equivalently the argument principle -- which is exactly the sorry in ConstructionTargets.Rouche. Queue rows already blocked on that same target: one-sorry-a92j05 and one-sorry-a94a10, both :blocked-on-construction-target. a97A08 makes three.", :parallel-to-a97a06 "This is the SECOND leverage finding of the night with the same shape: a single shared artifact gating multiple problems (there, a02J05's unreachable sinc library; here, one sorry in a reachable construction target). **Both say the same thing: the loop's remaining bottleneck is shared infrastructure, not individual problems.**", :frontier-retested "**I RE-TESTED THE FRONTIER RATHER THAN ACCEPTING THE LABEL, BECAUSE THREE PROBLEMS NOW DEPEND ON IT -- AND IT HELD.** Searched current Mathlib for Rouche, the argument principle, and analytic zero-counting in a disc: NO Rouche theorem, NO argument principle, and nothing beyond Splits.natDegree_eq_card_roots (global root count for split polynomials, no disc localisation). The :blocked-mathlib-frontier marking on rouche-root-count-transfer is CURRENT, not stale.", :consequence "If the Rouche construction target were closed, three problems become tractable at once. That makes it the highest-leverage single item in the corpus -- but it is a genuine Mathlib-frontier construction (argument principle), not an assembly, so it is not a cheap win."}, :classification :partial-blocked-on-construction-target, :axioms-verified-independently true, :metric-1-problems-solved 0, :axiom-verification "re-elaborated from a /tmp scratch copy: apm_a97A08_count_outer [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; apm_a97A08_main [propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] -- CONFIRMING the runner's own disclosure. One executable sorry remains (line 122).", :result :axiom-clean-partial, :commit "73b85263c2efc083c14e7892e478e2c49bbd0e8d", :sorry-delta-headline -2, :memory-used "e-codexpilot-bound-polynomial-sum-degree-by-a-common-summand-bound, for bounding the degree of the lower-order terms.", :metric-3-memories-surfaced 5, :declarations-newly-usable ["apm_a97A08_count_outer"], :sorry-delta-genuine-discharges -1, :search-audit "arm (a) carried the work and correctly identified ConstructionTargets/Rouche.lean and its remaining sorry; arms (b) Zulip (Rouche, argument principle, zero count disk, roots disk) and (c) arXiv both empty of formal constructions. Consistent with my independent Mathlib search.", :detail "a97A08 partial. One declaration closed axiom-clean by an elementary Cauchy-bound argument; the annulus bookkeeping is complete and the problem now reduces ENTIRELY to count_inner, which reduces entirely to the shared Rouche target."}, :runner "codex-6", :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:codex-pilot :partial :construction-target-leverage :rouche :frontier-retested-and-held :honest-sorryax-disclosure], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:30:07.644494410Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :problem, :ref/id "a97A08"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "09364db8-7fb1-4a00-938e-9a3b34c72aec"} {:evidence/body {:job-id "invoke-1785469907154-467-a2928a5f", :phase :outcome, :problem "a96A01", :row-kind :hard-proof-step, :runner-model :codex, :outcome {:recall-outcome-verbatim "[dispatch-recall-outcome=completed-with-memories]", :statement-preflight-result "0a/0b clean. Neither remaining target has a True conclusion; the only definition, quasiNorm f p = (int_{[0,1]} |f|^p)^(1/p), is genuine and not a placeholder; no inline (h : True) binders. Both remaining statements are substantive.", :metric-2-memories-saved 0, :metric-3-memories-used 1, :statement-preflight-run true, :classification :partial, :memory-shape-note "**ANOTHER INTERFACE-TRANSLATION MEMORY, NOT A MATHEMATICAL ONE.** This is now the recurring shape: the corpus proves most useful for connecting a file's own predicates to Mathlib's, rather than for supplying mathematics. Same as a95J05's two memories (strict/closed threshold bridge, a.e.-convergent subsequence API).", :frontier-assessment {:verdict :assembly-not-frontier, :reasoning "**APPLYING THE SHARPENED RULE -- COUNT ATTEMPTS THAT FAIL AT THE SAME POINT, NOT ATTEMPTS TOTAL.** This run ADVANCED the problem: three declarations closed, sorries 4 -> 2, and it produced the exponent-monotonicity spine (eLpNorm_le_eLpNorm_of_exponent_le, MemLp.mono_exponent) plus the monotone right-limit (MonotoneOn.tendsto_nhdsWithin_Ioo_right) that the remaining targets build on. Nothing failed twice at the same point. Both remaining obstructions come with CONCRETE NAMED ROUTES rather than frontier claims: ae_pos_of_limit_pos needs a filter-indexed dominated-convergence argument plus a variable-exponent squeeze; limit_ge_geometric_mean needs integrability control on the NEGATIVE PART of log |f| before Jensen can pass to the p -> 0+ limit. **This is a95A02's shape, not a95J08's** -- a long assembly, and it must not be marked as a frontier.", :negative-part-note "The named obstruction is precise and worth keeping: it is not `Jensen is missing` but `log |f| may fail to be integrable from below`. That is the actual mathematical content of the p -> 0+ geometric-mean limit, and it is the kind of specificity that makes a re-dispatch worthwhile rather than a re-run."}, :axioms-verified-independently true, :receipt-lateness "**RECORDED LATE, AND THAT IS ITSELF THE FINDING.** This result was read and summarised hours ago, but no receipt was ever written and the row stayed :status :dispatched with :receipt nil. It surfaced only because the park fired again. Reading a result is not processing it; the receipt is the artifact. Three other rows (a02J03, a94J04, a95A02) are in the same stale-:dispatched state and need the same reconciliation.", :metric-1-problems-solved 0, :axiom-verification "re-elaborated from a /tmp scratch copy, not trusting the runner: all three [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. Exactly 2 executable sorries remain (lines 141, 156). lake env lean exit 0.", :result :axiom-clean-partial, :commit "a960c44", :sorry-delta-headline -2, :memory-used "e-codexpilot-descend-through-eLpNorm-rpow-before-lintegral-rewrite, as an interface-normalization guide when translating quasiNorm through lpNorm/eLpNorm.", :error-recall "One error (Unknown constant ENNReal.ofReal_ne_zero); error-time recall surfaced no memory. Resolved by proving ENNReal.ofReal p != 0 by positivity. A nonexistent-declaration error is a cheap, high-frequency failure that error-time recall currently does not serve.", :metric-3-memories-surfaced 5, :declarations-newly-usable ["quasiNorm_eq_lpNorm" "quasiNorm_antitone" "quasiNorm_tendsto_exists"], :sorry-delta-genuine-discharges -2, :search-audit "arm (a) carried both proofs and its claims are consistent with the result; arms (b) Zulip (Lp norm p zero / geometric mean Lp / Lyapunov inequality / power mean inequality) and (c) arXiv manifest (power mean, generalized mean inequality) both genuinely empty. Loogle/LeanSearch found no packaged zero-exponent geometric-mean limit -- consistent with the remaining obstruction being real.", :detail "a96A01 partial. Sorries 4 -> 2, three declarations closed axiom-clean and independently verified. Route: generalized/power-mean monotonicity on a probability space plus existence of a one-sided limit for a bounded monotone function. Assembly, not frontier."}, :runner "codex-6", :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:codex-pilot :partial :memory-use :interface-normalisation :late-receipt :assembly-not-frontier], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:28:15.800677856Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :problem, :ref/id "a96A01"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "d93b18d6-b8cf-41a2-ba3d-ce943587e09b"} {:evidence/body {:recall-reason :timeout, :recall-status :recall-empty, :job-id "invoke-1785471894052-473-80a5fb14", :phase :offered, :problem "construction-deriv-ne-zero-of-injon", :recall-system :v1-enriched, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :pending-outcome, :memory-use/surfaced-ids [], :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/retrieval-to-use-ms 0, :memory-use/used-ids [], :memory-use/rejected-ids [], :memory-use/session-id "invoke-1785471894052-473-80a5fb14", :memory-use/cascade-id "dispatch-recall-empty-ecef9254-be87-4c58-aaad-e638a36ae410", :memory-use/surfaced-at "2026-07-31T04:24:55.181943080Z", :memory-use/decision-id "invoke-1785471894052-473-80a5fb14", :memory-use/surfacing-via [], :memory-use/inclusion-reasons [], :memory-use/unused-ids [], :memory-use/recorded-at "2026-07-31T04:24:55.181943080Z", :memory-use/rejection-reasons []}, :event :memory-use, :mint-candidates ["deriv" "none" "zero" "convergence"], :recall-query {:recall-system :v1-enriched, :term-sources [{:source :stdin-packet, :scope :mathematical-fields, :terms ["none" "convergence" "deriv" "deriv_ne_zero_of_injon" "differentiableon" "find" "hinj" "injon"]}], :terms ["deriv" "none" "zero" "convergence"], :query "deriv none zero convergence"}}, :evidence/session-id "invoke-1785471894052-473-80a5fb14", :evidence/tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-offered :recall-empty], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:24:55.196125528Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :apm-problem, :ref/id "construction-deriv-ne-zero-of-injon"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "e-24debb0a-8384-474c-8d1f-28b3700e2a0e"} {:evidence/body {:job-id "invoke-1785470932932-470-3e7d3fbd", :phase :outcome, :problem "a97A07", :row-kind :hard-proof-step, :runner-model :codex, :outcome {:recall-outcome-verbatim "[dispatch-recall-outcome=timeout]", :metric-2-memories-saved 0, :metric-3-memories-used :NOT-MEASURABLE, :metric-3-not-zero "**RECORDED AS :NOT-MEASURABLE, NOT AS ZERO.** Dispatch recall timed out, so no memory ids were supplied and nothing can be concluded about whether relevant memories exist. Writing 0 here would repeat the run-24 error precisely: that run's metric-3 zero was a :timeout, and I mis-diagnosed it as pattern-tier fragmentation and wrote the wrong finding into the whitepaper (correction receipt ae49c591).", :route "factor theorem / divided difference: defined the quotient (p - C (p.eval zeta)) /m (X - C zeta), then mul_divByMonic_eq_iff_isRoot, natDegree_divByMonic, and the degree of a product of linear factors.", :classification :partial, :axioms-verified-independently true, :metric-1-problems-solved 0, :axiom-verification "re-elaborated from a /tmp scratch copy: apm_a97A07_Q_polynomial_in_z and apm_a97A07_p_eval_zs both [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. Exactly 2 sorries remain (lines 72, 92). lake env lean exit 0.", :result :axiom-clean-partial, :store-checked-after "I checked the store rather than assuming, and rather than restarting reflexively: :7073 answered an entity fetch in 0.13s with http 200, host memory 14 GB available of 30 GB. The timeout was TRANSIENT. Joe authorised store restarts for memory pressure; the documented thresholds (2 consecutive recall failures / RSS > 10 GB / host available < 4 GB) were NOT met, so no restart was performed. Recording the non-action and its reason.", :remaining-targets "{\"apm_a97A07_P_polynomial\" \"expand the quotient in the monomial basis below degree n, show the coefficient functions are continuous on the root-free circle, integrate finitely many coefficients\", \"apm_a97A07_interpolates\" \"cancel the root factor at zs k, reparameterize t in [0,1] to circleIntegral's theta in [0,2pi], apply DifferentiableOn.circleIntegral_sub_inv_smul\"}", :commit "7f4b54af48cf864c8fcc3b1941887285a77c0504", :note-unused-hypothesis "The linter flags `hn : 0 < n` as unused in apm_a97A07_Q_polynomial_in_z. Per the a93J07 correction this is NOT a vacuity signal -- an unused hypothesis makes a theorem STRONGER. The 0a/0b preflight was run on this row before dispatch and was clean: no True conclusions, and the subjects (apm_a97A07_p, _Q, _P) are all genuine definitions.", :sorry-delta-headline -1, :metric-3-memories-surfaced :NOT-MEASURABLE, :declarations-newly-usable ["apm_a97A07_Q_polynomial_in_z" "apm_a97A07_p_eval_zs"], :sorry-delta-genuine-discharges -1, :recall-fix-validated "**THE RECALL-STATUS FIX IS WORKING AS DESIGNED, AND THIS RUN IS THE CLEANEST EVIDENCE YET.** The runner copied the typed banner VERBATIM, stated plainly that `dispatch recall timed out due to infrastructure unavailability; no dispatch-time memory IDs were supplied`, and DECLINED to infer a terrain gap from the absence. Before the typed banner, a timeout was indistinguishable from a genuine empty in the receipts. Both halves of the intended behaviour -- correct attribution AND declining the tempting inference -- are present.", :detail "a97A07 partial. Sorries 3 -> 2, two declarations closed axiom-clean and independently verified. Both remaining obstructions have concrete, named continuation routes rather than frontier claims."}, :runner "codex-6", :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:codex-pilot :partial :recall-timeout :metric-3-not-measurable :recall-banner-working-as-designed], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:21:26.714146632Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :problem, :ref/id "a97A07"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "bfeb6b27-c877-480b-9e52-b1725c5f4fff"} {:evidence/body {:job-id "invoke-1785470492377-469-c4cbe680", :phase :outcome, :problem "a97A06", :row-kind :hard-proof-step, :runner-model :codex, :outcome {:recall-outcome-verbatim "[dispatch-recall-outcome=completed-with-memories]", :structural-finding {:headline "**a97A06 IS BLOCKED ON A THEOREM THIS CORPUS HAS ALREADY PROVED, AND CANNOT REACH IT.**", :detail "The runner reports: `integration by parts reduces this to the Dirichlet sinc integral. That theorem exists in a02J05, but PROBLEM FILES ARE NOT IMPORTABLE MODULES; recreating its substantial Abel-regularization proof is still required.` **I verified the claim rather than taking it:** a02J05/lean/Main.lean has ZERO executable sorries and holds a 16-theorem sinc library, including `tendsto_integral_sinc_pi_div_two : Tendsto (fun R => int_0^R sinc) atTop (nhds (pi/2))` and `dirichlet_integral_improper`, plus the whole Abel-regularization chain (integral_exp_neg_mul_sinc_Ioi, tendsto_arctan_one_div_nhdsWithin, ...). That is precisely what apm_a97A06_main needs.", :same-defect-as "**THIS IS THE THIRD INSTANCE OF THE MODULE-PATH DEFECT TONIGHT.** ConstructionTargets had it (no lean_lib); YoungL2 had it (fixed in 7958c53, and the fix closed heatConv_L2_le in a96A04 within hours). Now a02J05's sinc library has it. The first two were single modules; this one says something larger: **the corpus systematically re-proves what it has already proved, because problems are leaves, not modules.**", :cost-visible-here "a97A06's runner spent its slot re-deriving arc estimates and then stopped at a wall that does not exist mathematically -- only structurally.", :recommended-repair "Do NOT make every problem file an importable lean_lib -- that would couple 145 problems into one build graph and make any problem's breakage everyone's. **PROMOTE the sinc/Dirichlet library into ConstructionTargets**, which already exists for exactly this purpose and is already on the module path. That converts a97A06_main from `recreate a substantial proof` into `import and apply`.", :decision-owner "joe", :generalisation-worth-measuring "Count how many blocked targets across the queue name a result that some OTHER problem file already proves axiom-clean. If that number is more than two or three, ConstructionTargets promotion is the highest-yield unblocking action available to this loop -- higher than any individual proof."}, :metric-2-memories-saved 0, :metric-3-memories-used 0, :classification :partial-blocked-on-corpus-internal-result, :axioms-verified-independently true, :metric-1-problems-solved 0, :axiom-verification "re-elaborated from a /tmp scratch copy, not trusting the runner: all three [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. Exactly 2 sorries remain (lines 14, 137). lake env lean exit 0.", :result :axiom-clean-partial, :remaining-targets "{\"apm_a97A06_F_analytic\" \"needs the second Taylor coefficient -2 identified for the double-dslope construction; genuine, not structural\", \"apm_a97A06_main\" \"structural only -- unblocked by promoting a02J05's sinc library to ConstructionTargets\"}", :commit "26368d445517ea7b90861ba96b5c6e9f162356ad", :metric-3-zero-is-legitimate "**THIS IS A REAL ZERO, NOT A FAILURE OR A TIMEOUT.** Recall COMPLETED (`[dispatch-recall-outcome=completed-with-memories]`) and the runner declined all five with specific per-memory reasons: parameterized Laplace transforms, compact-support Laplace, radial R3 integration, measurable-space diamond, Orlicz counterexample -- none touch a sinc-square contour integral. Distinguishing this from the run-24 :timeout zero is exactly what the typed recall banner was built for, and it works.", :sorry-delta-headline -3, :metric-3-memories-surfaced 5, :declarations-newly-usable ["apm_a97A06_integrable" "apm_a97A06_arc_exp_vanishes" "apm_a97A06_arc_inv_sq_vanishes"], :sorry-delta-genuine-discharges -3, :detail "a97A06 partial. Sorries 5 -> 2, three declarations closed axiom-clean and independently verified. The run's most valuable product is the structural finding: one of its two remaining targets is blocked not by mathematics but by the module path."}, :runner "codex-7", :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:codex-pilot :partial :module-path-defect :corpus-cannot-reach-itself :metric-3-legitimate-zero], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:21:00.988752410Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :problem, :ref/id "a97A06"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "061da818-83b2-4c4a-9985-37339195238f"} {:evidence/body {:recall-reason :timeout, :recall-status :recall-empty, :job-id "invoke-1785471544624-472-308f6c1d", :phase :offered, :problem "hard-problems-a95j07-lean-main-lean", :recall-system :v1-enriched, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :pending-outcom