vity" "e-codexpilot-derive-integrable-from-nonzero-bochner-integral" "e-codexpilot-extend-fin-partition-to-bounded-nat-sequence-for-telescoping"], :memory-use/recorded-at "2026-07-31T04:16:18.884634955Z", :memory-use/rejection-reasons []}, :recall-query {:recall-system :v1-enriched, :term-sources [{:source :stdin-packet, :scope :mathematical-fields, :terms ["apm_a97a08_f" "card" "filter" "roots" "line" "theorem" "none" "apm_a97a08_count_inner"]}], :terms ["count" "apm_a97a08_f" "outer" "card"], :query "count apm_a97a08_f outer card", :receipt-ranking {:enabled true, :alpha 0.5, :stats-found? false}}}, :evidence/session-id "invoke-1785471377736-471-acbcd206", :evidence/tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-offered], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:16:18.891494191Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :apm-problem, :ref/id "hard-problems-a97a08-lean-main-lean"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "e-fa99d629-1cf6-4bba-af6c-b891b2066333"} {:evidence/body {:job-id "invoke-1785470457961-468-ad547147", :phase :outcome, :problem "a96A04", :row-kind :hard-proof-step, :runner-model :codex, :outcome {:recall-outcome-verbatim "[dispatch-recall-outcome=completed-with-memories]", :metric-2-memories-saved 0, :metric-3-memories-used 2, :classification :partial-with-statement-defect-found, :statement-defect-found {:declaration "heatConv_contDiff", :mechanism :silent-api-drift-strengthening, :detail "The Lean asks `ContDiff R (top) (heatConv t f)`. In the CURRENT smoothness-index API the index type is `WithTop ENat` and `top` is notation for `omega`, which means REAL ANALYTIC -- strictly stronger than `infinity` (smooth). Verified independently against Mathlib source, not taken from the runner: FTaylorSeries.lean:112 `scoped[ContDiff] notation3 \"omega\" => (top : WithTop ENat)`, Defs.lean:90 `we denote (top : ENat) : WithTop ENat with infinity, and top : WithTop ENat with omega`, and Defs.lean:1165 `contDiff_omega_iff_analyticOnNhd : ContDiff k omega f <-> AnalyticOnNhd k f univ`. **THE PROBLEM ASKS FOR SMOOTH, NOT ANALYTIC**: problem.md says `u is smooth in the variable x`; informal-solution.md says `(a) u is smooth in x for t > 0` with the route `smoothness via DCT`; status.json says `part a: smoothness via DCT`; and the file's OWN docstring at line 81 says `u is smooth in x for t > 0` directly above a statement demanding analyticity. So the Lean statement is STRICTLY STRONGER THAN THE PROBLEM, and the runner spent its slot declaring an analytic-parameter-integral frontier that the problem never asked anyone to cross.", :why-nobody-edited-it "**THE SOURCE TEXT NEVER CHANGED; MATHLIB'S SEMANTICS MOVED UNDER IT.** When the smoothness index was ENat, `top` meant infinity = smooth. After the move to `WithTop ENat`, the identical token `top` means analytic. A statement can therefore go stale -- and get strictly harder -- with no edit to the file and no diff to review. Sorry counts, axiom censuses and signature diffs are all blind to it because nothing changed.", :proposed-repair "`ContDiff R (top)` -> `ContDiff R (infinity)`, the smooth class the problem asks for and which the informal solution's DCT route proves.", :decision-owner "joe", :precedent "a01A03 hit the IDENTICAL drift on 2026-07-30 and was repaired exactly this way -- its comment reads `Repair (2) was written as ContDiff R top f intending SMOOTH ... Corrected to ContDiff R infinity, the smooth test class actually intended.` There it was worse than a strengthening: compactly supported real-analytic functions on R are identically zero, so the hypothesis quantified over f = 0 alone and the statement became FALSE. **Precedent exists and is same-class; I am NOT treating it as standing authorisation.**", :corpus-sweep "grep for `ContDiff...top` across all 145 problem files returns exactly TWO hits: a01A03 (already diagnosed and repaired) and a96A04 (this one). The drift is contained -- there is no third instance."}, :axioms-verified-independently true, :metric-1-problems-solved 0, :axiom-verification "re-elaborated from a /tmp scratch copy, NOT trusting the runner: heatKernel_nonneg, heatKernel_integrable, heatConv_L2_le, heatKernel_integral all [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. Exactly 2 sorries remain (lines 87, 115). lake env lean exit 0.", :result :axiom-clean-partial, :remaining-targets "{\"heatConv_contDiff\" \"blocked pending the (top -> infinity) decision; under `infinity` the informal solution's DCT route applies and it is likely tractable\", \"heatConv_tendsto_L2\" \"genuinely open: needs integral Minkowski plus L2 translation continuity, or Plancherel. Not affected by the index question.\"}", :commit "a0a6f65298060d18b982949b6d0fd0ae2751e99b", :sorry-delta-headline -1, :younglib-payoff "**THE LAKEFILE FIX PAID WITHIN HOURS.** The runner reports `The repository's YoungL2 module closed heatConv_L2_le`. YoungL2 held an axiom-clean convolution_L2_contraction_of_probability_kernel that was UNREACHABLE until commit 7958c53 added its missing [[lean_lib]] stanza tonight. This is the first consumption of that module by another problem, and it discharged a declaration outright.", :metric-3-memories-surfaced 6, :declarations-newly-usable ["heatKernel_nonneg" "heatKernel_integrable" "heatConv_L2_le"], :sorry-delta-genuine-discharges -1, :search-audit "all three arms reported empty by the runner and the claims are consistent with the outcome: (a) found YoungL2's contraction and Mathlib's compact-support convolution regularity only; (b) Zulip empty for heat kernel / approximate identity / Young / convolution L2; (c) arXiv manifest returned four unrelated Banach/Fourier-algebra papers, no anchor.", :memory-finding {:headline "**A MEMORY WAS COUNTED AS USED, TRANSFERRED ITS FACT CORRECTLY, AND STILL PRODUCED THE WRONG DECISION.**", :memory "e-codexpilot-distinguish-ContDiff-top-analytic-from-ContDiff-infinity-smooth", :provenance "promoted from the a01A03 diagnosis earlier the same day", :what-happened "The memory surfaced for a96A04 and the runner used it -- correctly -- to establish that `top` means analytic. It then drew the OPPOSITE operational conclusion from a01A03's: a01A03 concluded `therefore the statement is mis-stated, repair it to infinity`; a96A04 concluded `therefore this is a hard analytic construction` and declared a frontier. **The memory carries the FACT but not its CONSEQUENT.** It says what `top` means; it does not say that when the informal problem asks for smoothness, `top` is a MIS-STATEMENT to repair rather than a frontier to assault.", :missing-discriminator "The memory also omits the cheap check that settles it: COMPARE THE LEAN INDEX AGAINST problem.md. One grep for `smooth` in a96A04/problem.md decides the question. The memory should carry the check, not just the distinction.", :metric-consequence "**metric-3 counts this as a memory USED, and by any mechanical definition it was.** But the run it informed reached the wrong conclusion and burned a runner slot on an unnecessary frontier. So `memories used` is NOT the same as `memories used well`, and our headline metric-3 number does not currently distinguish them. This deflates the metric-3 story somewhat and is recorded for exactly that reason.", :amendment-owed "amend the memory to carry the consequent and the problem.md check -- a memory AMENDMENT, which the promotion pipeline cannot apply; must be done by hand."}, :detail "a96A04 partial. Sorries 3 -> 2, three declarations closed axiom-clean and independently verified. The run's real product is not the partial: it is (i) the first consumption of the newly-importable YoungL2 module, which closed heatConv_L2_le outright, (ii) a statement defect in heatConv_contDiff caused by silent Mathlib API drift, and (iii) evidence that a correctly-surfaced, correctly-used memory can still drive a wrong decision when it records a fact without its consequent."}, :runner "codex-6", :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:codex-pilot :partial :statement-defect :api-drift :memory-use :memory-used-to-wrong-conclusion :younglib-payoff :metric-3-caveat], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:11:57.511535662Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :problem, :ref/id "a96A04"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "e9d008be-b34f-40a4-a00e-e6a16d245122"} {:evidence/body {:recall-reason :timeout, :recall-status :recall-empty, :job-id "invoke-1785470932932-470-3e7d3fbd", :phase :offered, :problem "hard-problems-a97a07-lean-main-lean", :recall-system :v1-enriched, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :pending-outcome, :memory-use/surfaced-ids [], :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/retrieval-to-use-ms 0, :memory-use/used-ids [], :memory-use/rejected-ids [], :memory-use/session-id "invoke-1785470932932-470-3e7d3fbd", :memory-use/cascade-id "dispatch-recall-empty-4141ba78-b707-43aa-adb3-b0fe7620f5ac", :memory-use/surfaced-at "2026-07-31T04:08:54.622452591Z", :memory-use/decision-id "invoke-1785470932932-470-3e7d3fbd", :memory-use/surfacing-via [], :memory-use/inclusion-reasons [], :memory-use/unused-ids [], :memory-use/recorded-at "2026-07-31T04:08:54.622452591Z", :memory-use/rejection-reasons []}, :event :memory-use, :mint-candidates ["polynomial" "convergence" "natdegree" "line"], :recall-query {:recall-system :v1-enriched, :term-sources [{:source :stdin-packet, :scope :mathematical-fields, :terms ["convergence" "line" "p_poly" "theorem" "aeval" "analyticon" "apm_a97a07_p" "complex"]}], :terms ["polynomial" "convergence" "natdegree" "line"], :query "polynomial convergence natdegree line"}}, :evidence/session-id "invoke-1785470932932-470-3e7d3fbd", :evidence/tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-offered :recall-empty], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:08:54.635318251Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :apm-problem, :ref/id "hard-problems-a97a07-lean-main-lean"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "e-32d38437-54c8-45a9-851f-342774ea6c9b"} {:evidence/body {:phase :preflight-block, :problem "a96A02", :row-kind :hard-proof-step, :runner-model :none-never-dispatched, :outcome {:proposed-repair "Either (a) supply the real piecewise-linear spike construction, or (b) make spikeFunction genuinely opaque -- an axiomatised specification, or the intended properties taken as hypotheses -- so both theorems have content. As written neither can be honestly discharged: one is trivial, one is false.", :caught-by :step-0-vacuity-preflight-BEFORE-dispatch, :placeholder "def spikeFunction : R -> R := 0", :metric-2-memories-saved 0, :defect-class :scaffold-placeholder, :defect-mechanism :constant-subject-definition, :metric-3-memories-used :NOT-MEASURABLE-no-dispatch-no-recall, :target-1-verdict :vacuously-true, :classification :blocked-placeholder-subject, :predictive-catch true, :metric-1-problems-solved 0, :sorry-delta-real 0, :target-2-verdict :FALSE, :result :not-dispatched, :decision-owner "joe", :preflight-generalisation "The step-0 check must include: does the conclusion's SUBJECT unfold to a bare constant? A non-True conclusion about a placeholder subject is just as vacuous as a True conclusion, and the a96A02 targets show it can also be FALSE -- the placeholder makes the negative statement unprovable, not just the positive one trivial.", :targets-about-placeholder ["spikeFunction_holderWith" "spikeFunction_not_absolutelyContinuous"], :target-genuine ["spike_height_slope_bound"], :detail "a96A02 NOT dispatched. `def spikeFunction : R -> R := 0` -- the constant zero function -- and TWO of the three sorried targets are ABOUT it. (1) spikeFunction_holderWith asserts exists A > 0 with |spikeFunction x - spikeFunction y| <= A|x-y|^(1/2); under the constant zero the LHS is identically 0, so the target is TRIVIALLY TRUE and a runner could close it with `positivity`-grade steps and report CLEAN -- the a95J03 failure mode exactly. (2) spikeFunction_not_absolutelyContinuous asserts exists eps > 0 with eps <= sum |spikeFunction(b i) - spikeFunction(a i)|; under the constant zero that sum is identically 0, so the target is FALSE -- the constant function IS absolutely continuous. ONE TARGET VACUOUS, ONE FALSE, BOTH FROM THE SAME PLACEHOLDER. Only spike_height_slope_bound is genuine: it is pure arithmetic ((1/n) * (2*(n+1)) <= 4 for n >= 1) and does not mention spikeFunction. **THE FILE CLAIMS AN OPACITY IT DOES NOT HAVE**: its header (lines 23-25, 46) says the definition is left `opaque ... with a precise specification of its values` and `We define it opaquely since the full piecewise-linear construction` [is hard], but line 49 is literally `def spikeFunction : R -> R := 0` and NO specification is stated anywhere in the file. The prose describes an intended repair that the code does not implement. This is the second consecutive row where the step-0 preflight (`is the CONCLUSION itself True or trivially satisfiable, and does its SUBJECT unfold to a placeholder`) blocked a false CLEAN before a runner slot was spent -- a95J06 was the first."}, :verified-by "claude-9"}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/overnight", :evidence/tags [:codex-pilot :preflight-block :vacuity :placeholder-subject :predictive-catch :statement-defect :not-dispatched], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T04:04:11.591688540Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :problem, :ref/id "a96A02"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "087f0667-a5c0-4878-81c8-4e50840879e8"} {:evidence/body {:event :memory-use, :recall-status :ok, :job-id "invoke-1785470492377-469-c4cbe680", :phase :offered, :problem "hard-problems-a97a06-lean-main-lean", :recall-system :v1-enriched, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :pending-outcome, :memory-use/surfaced-ids ["e-codexpilot-prove-Laplace-analyticity-by-conjugate-Holder-and-local-derivative-domination" "e-codexpilot-sp