on matters, because 'the whole lemma is blocked' would have hidden a proved branch. THE DECISION WAS PRE-COMMITTED AND I AM HONOURING IT AS WRITTEN. Three independent attempts (afda168b, 3dd86554, this one) all failed on the general case. That matches the rouche precedent of three, and scribe 34's rule that attempt history be recorded before the transition. **Two problems tonight had named gaps CONSTRUCTED on a later attempt -- a93A04 and a95A02 -- so I checked myself against loosening the bar; but rouche went three and stayed blocked, and the alternative is re-dispatching a confirmed gap indefinitely.** The runner reached the same conclusion independently and labelled its own outcome :blocked-mathlib-frontier. EVIDENCE QUALITY IS UNUSUALLY GOOD FOR A FRONTIER CALL: three failed attempts; a Zulip 'Discrete analysis' thread stating explicitly that Young's inequality and substantial convolution infrastructure are MISSING from Mathlib; a literature anchor verified against the local arXiv manifest (Soudsky, 'Minkowski Integral Inequality Revisited', 1704.08922) which supplies the mathematical scaffold but no Lean implementation; and a precise statement of what is missing. **a94A03 REMAINS BLOCKED**, and its dependency is now on the 1 < p < infinity case specifically. METRIC 3 MEASURABLE: 5 surfaced, 3 used -- the frontier memory again 'correctly identified the general Jensen-Tonelli bridge', and **the two scope-guard memories were consumed for the THIRD time**, this time explicitly 'as a caution against UNDERSTATING this construction frontier' and 'to avoid misclassifying the missing weighted inequality as mere API adaptation'."}, :recall-system :v3-typed-recall-status, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :outcome-recorded, :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/used-ids ["e-codexpilot-prove-general-probability-kernel-Lp-contraction-by-integral-Young" "e-codexpilot-bound-automatic-frontier-descent-when-a-leaf-recurses" "e-codexpilot-bound-the-interface-adapter-heurist