able_of_isOpen for countability -- rather than manually sorting arbitrary intervals, which is what attempt 2 had assumed was required. **WITH a93A04 THAT IS 2 FOR 2 ON NAMED GAPS BEING CONSTRUCTED, AND IT BEARS DIRECTLY ON A DECISION I PRE-COMMITTED THIS HOUR.** I have a95J08 attempt 3 in flight with the rule that a third failure marks it :blocked-mathlib-frontier. That rule came from scribe 34 and matches the rouche precedent of three independent failures -- and I am NOT loosening it on the strength of two counterexamples, because rouche went three and stayed genuinely blocked. But the distinction is now sharp: **'Mathlib has no packaged X' should be read as 'nobody has assembled X yet', which is a claim about effort, not about possibility.** A frontier is what survives repeated attempts, not what a search failed to find. REMAINING for ac_lusin_condition_N, now a concrete four-step plan on top of the proved decomposition: identify sInf/sSup endpoints for each open component intersected with [0,1]; bound the outer measure of its image by the integral of the norm of deriv f between those endpoints; sum over the now-proved countable pairwise-disjoint family; apply Integrable.tendsto_setIntegral_nhds_zero. Part (c)'s Borel-versus-completion defect is untouched and still needs Joe. METRIC 3: NOT MEASURABLE, recall timed out."}, :recall-system :v3-typed-recall-status, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :outcome-recorded, :memory-use/surfaced-ids [], :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/used-ids [], :memory-use/decision-id "invoke-1785468518124-461-33b542ab", :memory-use/measurable? false, :memory-use/recall-outcome :timeout}, :event :memory-use, :runner "codex-7", :dispatch-mode :duree-overnight-parallel}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree", :evidence/tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-outcome :codex-pilot :duree-run :blocked-with-partial :gap-constructed :overnight], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T03:41:09.879860Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/