E JUNK-VALUE UMBRELLA AND I AM NOT FOLDING IT IN.** Every totalisation case tonight -- integral_undef, deriv, ENNReal top -- turned on Lean assigning a junk value to an undefined operation. Nothing is totalised here. The hypothesis set is simply too weak TOPOLOGICALLY: empty interior does not prevent a null complement. Scribe pass 33 corrected me for lumping four mechanisms under one cause, and pass 34 has the taxonomy in hand, so this is recorded as `:defect-mechanism :missing-topological-hypothesis` and FLAGGED for its judgement rather than generalised by me. **AN ELEGANT SIMPLIFICATION WORTH CAPTURING SEPARATELY: the fat-set proof AVOIDS a bespoke Smith-Volterra construction entirely.** Remove the countable dense rationals from [0,1], leaving a measurable set of volume 1; use INNER REGULARITY of Lebesgue measure to extract a positive-measure compact subset; then any interior point would yield a rational inside that compact subset, contradicting its construction. Four steps against a hand-rolled nested-interval construction. METRIC 3: NOT MEASURABLE, recall timed out, reported verbatim."}, :recall-system :v3-typed-recall-status, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :outcome-recorded, :memory-use/surfaced-ids [], :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/used-ids [], :memory-use/decision-id "invoke-1785465399678-446-4d291d8d", :memory-use/measurable? false, :memory-use/recall-outcome :timeout, :memory-use/runner-reported-status-verbatim? true}, :event :memory-use, :runner "codex-6", :dispatch-mode :duree-overnight-parallel}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree", :evidence/tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-outcome :codex-pilot :duree-run :blocked-with-partial :statement-false :new-mechanism :overnight], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T02:44:13.176425Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :apm-problem, :ref/id "a94J02"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "f74ec63f-b997-4606-9e4e-84e531d715cc"} {: