ithmetic including the telescoping sum", :classification :blocked-all-targets-false, :metric-1-problems-solved 31, :counterexample "atomic mu = sum of Diracs at x_m = 1 - 1/(m+2); f(x_m) = 1/(m+1); f in L2 since sum 1/(m+1)^2 converges; x_m^n f(x_m) >= 2^-n/(m+1) harmonic-divergent so every monomial integral is junk-zero", :repair-applied false, :sorry-delta-headline 0, :no-commit true, :sharper-detail "p(X) = 1 - X gives p(x_m) f(x_m) = 1/((m+1)(m+2)), genuinely INTEGRABLE with telescoping integral 1, not 0 - the conclusion is refuted on an instance where the integral IS defined", :arm-that-paid :components-diagnosis-only, :metric-3-exclude-from-benchmark true, :declarations-newly-usable 0, :repair-deferred-to :joe, :detail "a94A04 BLOCKED: both statements are FALSE for arbitrary mu. Sorries 3 -> 3, no files changed, no commit -- verified, working tree clean. Ninth run tonight to diagnose without touching the file. I READ both statements and confirmed the defect: each quantifies over an ARBITRARY mu : Measure R with NO finiteness constraint, and neither assumes integrability of the monomial products. COUNTEREXAMPLE, whose arithmetic I checked: take x_m = 1 - 1/(m+2) in [1/2, 1) and the ATOMIC measure mu = sum of Diracs at x_m, with f(x_m) = 1/(m+1) and f = 0 elsewhere. Then sum 1/(m+1)^2 converges so f is in L^2 and measurable; but x_m^n f(x_m) >= 2^-n/(m+1) because x_m >= 1/2, and the harmonic sum diverges, so every monomial product is NON-INTEGRABLE and integral_undef makes every asserted monomial integral 0. The hypothesis is therefore satisfied vacuously, while f is nonzero at every atom and so is not zero almost everywhere. **THE SECOND HALF IS SHARPER THAN VACUITY AND IS WORTH SEPARATING.** For orthogonal_to_polynomials take p(X) = 1 - X. Then p(x_m) = 1/(m+2), so p(x_m) f(x_m) = 1/((m+1)(m+2)), which IS integrable, and the telescoping sum gives integral 1, NOT 0. **So the conclusion is refuted on an instance where the integral is genuinely defined and computable** -- the hypothesis is vacuous, but the falsity is real rather than merely unconstrained. That is a stronger form of evidence than the vacuity cases recorded earlier tonight, and I have added the corresponding check to the loop: when a hypothesis is found vacuous, ask whether some INSTANCE of the conclusion is computable and false, which upgrades 'vacuous' to 'refuted'. CLASSIFICATION: integral_undef mechanism, under scribe 33's umbrella 'missing semantic-domain guards admit degenerate witnesses'. PROOF STATUS: ARGUED -- the counterexample is described and I checked the arithmetic, but it is not formalised. REPAIRS the runner offers, and they differ per target: for the standalone polynomial lemma, require integrability of every monomial product, or fold integrability into the moment hypothesis; for the main theorem, require FINITE measure on [0,1], e.g. mu (Icc 0 1) < infinity, after which L^2 is contained in L^1 on the restricted measure and the intended Stone-Weierstrass / Lp-density proof becomes valid. METRIC 3: NOT MEASURABLE, recall timed out."}, :recall-system :v3-typed-recall-status, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :outcome-recorded, :memory-use/surfaced-ids [], :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/used-ids [], :memory-use/decision-id "invoke-1785464465577-442-69142f39", :memory-use/measurable? false, :memory-use/recall-outcome :timeout, :memory-use/runner-reported-status-verbatim? true}, :event :memory-use, :runner "codex-6", :dispatch-mode :duree-overnight-parallel}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree", :evidence/tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-outcome :codex-pilot :duree-run :statement-false :vacuous-hypothesis-family :overnight], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T02:28:52.410219Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :apm-problem, :ref/id "a94A04"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "782070a0-17b3-478c-a5e6-243c797e73d2"} {:evidence/body {:recall-reason :timeout, :reca