ty to refute a statement). The memory is now load-bearing in both directions and was used forward within hours of being amended backward. It also used reduce-probability-kernel-L2-contraction-to-young CONCEPTUALLY and reported a precise BOUNDARY on it: the memory accurately identifies the missing Young estimate, but this target needs general finite p while the memory and the repository's YoungL2.lean cover only p = 2. **A memory reported as accurate-but-too-narrow is a better signal than a bare hit or miss.** REMAINING: prove eLpNorm (gaussConv t f) p volume <= eLpNorm f p volume for all 1 <= p < infinity. Mathlib's scalar Holder/Jensen/Fubini lemmas do not package the integral Minkowski/Young step; once available, combine with Continuous.compMeasurePreservingLp and Gaussian scaling plus dominated convergence. Genuine Mathlib gap, not a statement defect."}, :recall-system :v3-typed-recall-status, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :outcome-recorded, :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/error-time {:invocations 1, :hits 0}, :memory-use/used-ids ["e-codexpilot-derive-integrable-from-nonzero-bochner-integral" "e-codexpilot-reduce-probability-kernel-L2-contraction-to-young"], :memory-use/measurable? true, :memory-use/forward-direction-use "derive-integrable-from-nonzero-bochner-integral used FORWARD (integrability from nonzero integral) while claude-9 amended it TWICE tonight for the REVERSE refutation direction", :memory-use/recall-outcome :completed-with-memories, :memory-use/boundary-reported "reduce-probability-kernel-L2-contraction-to-young is accurate but scoped to p=2; this target needs general finite p", :memory-use/decision-id "invoke-1785464073951-441-1c05a75c"}, :event :memory-use, :runner "codex-6", :dispatch-mode :duree-overnight-parallel}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree", :evidence/tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-outcome :codex-pilot :duree-run :blocked-with-partial :mathlib-frontier :stale-scaffold-guidance :memory-used :overnight],