alytic order, otherwise applying zero persistence to F n z - F n y on a punctured neighbourhood to contradict injectivity. VERIFIED: ZERO signature changes, 3 declarations before and after; placeholder scan clean; all three re-elaborate as [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. Headline -3 and genuine -3 agree. **I ADDED AN UNUSED-PARAMETER VACUITY CHECK THIS TURN AND THIS RUN IMMEDIATELY REFINED IT.** The run reported an unused-parameter warning for hz0, and a95J03's vacuous close had shown up with unused hypotheses (hN, hz), so I checked. Result: hz0 IS used in one declaration (line 67, via hOmega.mem_nhds hz0) and unused in hurwitz_eventually_nonvanishing_on_sphere -- where it is simply REDUNDANT, because hclosed : closedBall z0 r subset Omega already implies z0 in Omega. **The conclusion there is substantive: for all n eventually, for all z on the sphere, F n z /= 0.** **SO THE CHECK AS I WROTE IT WAS WRONG AND I AM CORRECTING IT.** An unused hypothesis makes a theorem STRONGER, not vacuous -- it proves more with less. a95J03's vacuity came from its CONCLUSION being about a placeholder constant function; the unused hypotheses were a SYMPTOM, not the cause. The correct check is: **is the CONCLUSION substantive -- does its subject unfold to something real -- with unused hypotheses only as corroborating evidence.** Applying the symptom as the test would flag every redundantly-stated theorem in the corpus and miss any vacuous one whose hypotheses happen to be used. SEARCH: arm (a) local carried it -- TendstoLocallyUniformlyOn.differentiableOn, DiffContOnCl.ball_subset_image_closedBall, AnalyticAt.eventually_eq_zero_or_eventually_ne_zero, AnalyticOnNhd.eqOn_of_preconnected_of_eventuallyEq, ENat.ne_top_iff_exists. Loogle and LeanSearch returned no direct target theorem; arms (b) and (c) were not needed. METRIC 3 MEASURABLE: 5 surfaced, 0 used, each declined with an individual substantive reason."}, :recall-system :v3-typed-recall-status, :memory-use {:memory-use/sta