potheses on the kernel sections, or reformulation with nonnegative `lintegral` bounds; the two helper lemmas additionally need integrability assumptions on their displayed integrands. That is a premise rewrite on three targets -- larger than a restatement -- so it is Joe's call, not mine. METRIC 3: 5 surfaced, 0 used. Best discrimination: prove-weak-L2-convergence-by-Vitali-on-products-over-infinite-measure was declined with the note that its infinite-measure warning is DIRECTIONALLY RELATED but the targets fail EARLIER, through integral_undef -- a near-miss judged on where in the argument the failure occurs, which is a finer discrimination than relevance."}, :recall-system :v3-typed-recall-status, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :outcome-recorded, :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/used-ids [], :memory-use/decision-id "invoke-1785457061590-420-9110d0ac", :memory-use/error-time {:invocations 0, :hits 0}, :memory-use/measurable? true, :memory-use/recall-outcome :completed-with-memories, :memory-use/best-discrimination "weak-L2-Vitali declined as directionally related but the targets fail EARLIER via integral_undef - a near-miss judged on WHERE in the argument the failure occurs"}, :event :memory-use, :runner "codex-6", :dispatch-mode :duree-overnight-parallel}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree", :evidence/tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-outcome :codex-pilot :duree-run :statement-false :junk-value-family :overnight], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T00:24:14.183297Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :apm-problem, :ref/id "a02J01"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "659233e8-9080-464b-9ea9-3f4e957f6556"} {:evidence/body {:job-id "invoke-1785457030310-419-0dd760eb", :row-kind :hard-proof-step, :phase :outcome, :problem "a01J06-jensen-zero-count", :runner-model :codex, :outcome {:verified-by "claude-9", :metric-3-status :MEASURABLE-recall-completed, :metric-3-memories-used 0, :div