and the corpus also holds record-real-analysis-riemann-darboux-recall-terrain under math/riemann-darboux-api. Recall surfaced 0 and the runner reported no dispatch-time memories. Probing the FIXED seam directly: the filter now works correctly (rows are filtered to :evidence/type :memory), but the TRIPLE tier 'indicator riemann integrable' returns 7 rows, ALL of them zai-lane memories with UUID ids and NONE of them codex-lane; the codex memories appear only at the SINGLES tier - 'riemann' alone surfaces record-real-analysis-riemann-darboux-recall-terrain among 5. So the ladder's stopping condition is the remaining question: it halts at the first tier with candidates, and 'non-empty' is not the same as 'useful'. I have NOT probed the pattern-proposal step, which sits between the search rows and the offered memories, so I cannot yet say whether the ladder actually stopped at the triple tier or continued and still found nothing. Recording that as an open question rather than guessing. FIFTH INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION of the standing pattern: the runner found the right lemma on its own, using a declaration the corpus has a memory about, without the memory being offered. SEARCH: arm (a) carried it; a Loogle pattern query failed to parse ('Unknown identifier .indicator') while name queries MeasureTheory.integral_indicator_one and IsCompact.measure_lt_top returned those exact declarations - another instance of name-guessing beating pattern search. LeanSearch also returned relevant results, a second consecutive break in the streak."}, :recall-system :v1-ladder-filter-fixed, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :outcome-recorded, :memory-use/surfaced-ids [], :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/error-time {:invocations 2, :hits 0}, :memory-use/used-ids [], :memory-use/runner-used-the-documented-declaration "riemann_lebesgue_sandwich", :memory-use/relevant-memories-existed ["e-codexpilot-bridge-darboux-cells-to-lebesgue-integral-by-telescoping" "e-codexpilot-record-real-analy