2"], :s9-confidence-was "high", :divergence :false-as-stated-lean-junk-value-nonintegrable-integral, :detail "a95A08 jensen_exp_circle: BLOCKED false-as-stated, then REPAIRED directly under Joe's standing authorisation. The statement integrates Real.log (g theta) with no hypothesis that log-of-g is integrable, and Lean's Bochner integral of a non-integrable function is 0. Runner's counterexample, verified by reading the statement: g = 1 at theta = 0 and exp(-1/theta) otherwise on [0,2pi] is measurable, positive everywhere, bounded by 1 and integrable, so it satisfies EVERY hypothesis; but log (g theta) = -1/theta a.e., not integrable near 0, so the left side collapses to exp 0 = 1 while the right side is strictly below 1 because 0 < g < 1 a.e. SAME FAMILY as ledger #4 (a01A02): a LEAN JUNK-VALUE CONVENTION -- toReal of top = 0 there, integral of non-integrable = 0 here -- silently converting an unbounded quantity into a harmless one. That is now a named recurring family with two confirmed instances, and it is semi-greppable. REPAIR: added hg_log_int : IntegrableOn (fun theta => Real.log (g theta)) (Icc 0 (2*pi)) volume, exactly what the runner specified. Statement change only -- builds exit 0, sorry count unchanged at 4, no call sites affected (apm-lean commit follows). THIRD S9 FALSE NEGATIVE, and the worst of them: S9 returned :ok with HIGH confidence for this row, writing that the final intended statements agree with Lean and the exam. Revised S9 scoreboard: 3 confirmed false negatives among 57 :ok verdicts (a01A11, a01A07, a95A08). All three were found by a proof attempt or by a targeted mechanical sweep, never by the reading pass -- which is the honest limit of statement reconciliation as an instrument. SWEEP: built a detector for this family (statement integrates log / inverse / rpow with no matching Integrable hypothesis), VALIDATED it against the pre-repair a95A08 where it correctly fires, and ran it over the 66 remaining untouched rows: ZERO hits. So this family's remaining exposure in the untouched tail is nil, within the detector's limits -- it requires a visible integral sign and would miss lintegral forms and the hypothesis-strength family entirely. EXPERIMENT: datum 2 of 10 in the well-posed-row run, and it turned out NOT to be well-posed -- a95A08 was prioritised for its available Schwarz lemma, not because it had been audited or repaired. The seven rows I actually repaired are still ahead in the queue."}, :recall-system :v1-enriched, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :outcome-recorded, :memory-use/surfaced-ids [], :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/used-ids [], :memory-use/decision-id "invoke-1785382213987-297-aa0f7e6a", :memory-use/unused-ids [], :memory-use/error-time {:invocations 0, :hits 0, :note "no compile errors; found by semantic inspection before implementation"}}, :event :memory-use}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/cron-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-outcome :codex-pilot :cron-lane :faithfulness :hard-proof-step], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T03:35:04.736786Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :apm-problem, :ref/id "a95A08"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "93926277-6156-4ced-a788-d82783968a62"} {:evidence/body {:recall-status :recall-empty, :job-id "invoke-1785382213987-297-aa0f7e6a", :phase :offered, :problem "hard-problems-a95a08-lean-main-lean", :recall-system :v1-enriched, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :pending-outcome, :memory-use/surfaced-ids [], :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/retrieval-to-use-ms 0, :memory-use/used-ids [], :memory-use/rejected-ids [], :memory-use/session-id "invoke-1785382213987-297-aa0f7e6a", :memory-use/cascade-id "dispatch-recall-888b4391-da6d-4ae1-9a91-09e772c8d2cd", :memory-use/surfaced-at "2026-07-30T03:30:14.630067879Z", :memory-use/decision-id "invoke-1785382213987-297-aa0f7e6a", :memory-use/inclusion-reasons [], :memory-use/unused-ids [], :memo