= x^(-3/4) on (0,1], 0 elsewhere. Ground control MACHINE-CHECKED the two load-bearing integrability facts (/tmp/a01A06_num.lean, exit 0): (1) integral over (0,1) of x^(-3/4) = 4, so g IS in L1 as OrliczBound requires; (2) x^(-3/2) is NOT integrable on Ioo 0 1 via integrableOn_Ioo_rpow_iff, i.e. g^2 is not integrable -- which is precisely the refutation of orlicz_bound_implies_L2. HAND-VERIFIED, not machine-checked, and flagged as such: the Young-Fenchel step gf <= exp f + g log g - g giving integral of gf <= 1 + 12 - 4 = 9 < 10, so OrliczBound g 10 holds (the value 12 for the integral of g log g follows from the standard integral of x^a log x = -1/(a+1)^2 at a = -3/4, giving -3/4 times -16); and the distribution identity measure{g > lam} = lam^(-4/3) for lam >= 1, which no C exp(-alpha lam) can bound since polynomial decay beats exponential. I attempted a Lean proof of that last point and abandoned it as over-engineered for an elementary fact -- recording the boundary rather than implying full formalisation. SORRY ACCOUNTING: the runner reported 4 -> 4 and my lexical grep said 5; the runner is RIGHT -- there are 4 real sorries (lines 97, 117, 139, 166) plus one prose mention of the word on line 43. Second time today the lexical meter has overstated against a correct runner report, which is exactly why receipts now carry :sorry-delta-real and :sorry-delta-lexical separately. Verified: tree clean but for the pre-existing untracked .bak, HEAD unchanged at 8df8148, no commit. REPAIR IS JOE'S CALL: strengthen the hypothesis to genuine exponential integrability of g, or weaken both conclusions to the corresponding L-log-L / entropy and POLYNOMIAL-tail statements. PROCESS NOTE, and it is mine not the runner's: this bellback arrived at roughly 21:30 BST and I did not run the per-row protocol on it, so the row sat :dispatched and verification backpressure correctly gate-closed the 21:30Z, 22:30Z, 23:30Z and 00:30Z fires. The loop did exactly what it is designed to do; no run