 on the accumulated error. Minimal witness in l2(N): f0 = e0, f1 = (1/2)e0 + (sqrt3/2)e1, fn = en for n>=2. Ground control checked ADMISSIBILITY carefully, because the example is knife-edge: all norms are 1, and the hypothesis at (n,m)=(0,1) requires |<f0,f1>| <= 2^-1, with the example giving EXACTLY 1/2 -- admissible, saturating the bound. All other pairs are orthogonal. Gram-Schmidt at m=1 projects out the e0 component leaving (sqrt3/2)e1, which normalises to e1, so ||f1 - e1|| = ||(1/2)e0 + (sqrt3/2 - 1)e1|| = sqrt(1/4 + 7/4 - sqrt3) = sqrt(2 - sqrt3) = 0.5176..., against the claimed bound of 0.5. WHAT WAS MACHINE-CHECKED vs HAND-CHECKED, stated precisely: the deciding inequality sqrt(2 - sqrt3) > 1/2 was machine-checked in Lean (/tmp/a01A05_num.lean, exit 0). The l2 construction itself was NOT formalised -- it requires infinitely many dimensions, since near-orthogonality of the tail cannot be realised in finite dimension, and building it in Lean is hours of work for a result whose structure is elementary. The Gram-Schmidt computation and hypothesis-admissibility were verified by hand, step by step. THE HONEST LIMIT THIS ROW PUTS ON THE S9 CASE: mechanisms 3, 4 and 6 (variable not included; .toReal with no ne-top; Fin n -> R used as Euclidean space) are greppable and a static scan finds them free. THIS ONE IS NOT. Nothing about the statement is syntactically suspicious -- it is well-typed, well-scoped, uses the right ambient structures, and is simply false by a margin of about 0.018. It required attempting the proof and constructing a knife-edge counterexample. So S9 reduces the cost of the tail but does NOT remove the need to attempt rows: of 5 statement defects so far, 4 were greppable and 1 was not. RECALL FINDING, the sharpest this lane has produced: the surfaced-id set for this row is IDENTICAL, in the same order, to the set surfaced for a01A02 -- five ids, verified equal element by element. Those are unrelated problems (a weak-L2 distribution estimate vs Gram-Schmidt orthonormalisation in a Hilbert space). Recall is therefore not discriminating on problem content. Note it is NOT a constant response either, since a00J05 and a00J06 returned genuinely empty post-fix, so the working hypothesis for claude-4's investigation is COARSE-GRAINED matching -- at terrain or domain level rather than problem content. n=2 and both are analysis rows, so this is a hypothesis to test, not a conclusion. Verified: tree clean but for the pre-existing .bak, HEAD unchanged at 8df8148, sorry count 2 -> 2, no commit -- as claimed."}, :recall-system :v1-enriched, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :outcome-recorded, :memory-use/surfaced-ids ["e-0e4e32fe-54af-451b-b302-17aa521891fd" "e-30e87097-f843-4341-81c0-a49ee7ce0ef4" "e-afb1eae8-284f-4551-8c49-d0babd83a780" "e-e7805bcc-6d9f-492d-9bd5-b12d0fbb9dde" "e-ff95cfd3-c645-4b64-afa1-46605015bb00"], :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/used-ids [], :memory-use/decision-id "invoke-1785353412527-288-08144a51", :memory-use/error-time {:invocations 0, :hits 0, :note "no compile errors beyond the two expected sorry warnings"}, :memory-use/identical-to-job "invoke-1785342613132-282-b20c35fc"}, :event :memory-use}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/cron-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-outcome :codex-pilot :cron-lane :faithfulness :hard-proof-step :recall-precision], :evidence/at "2026-07-29T19:34:28.603866Z", :evidence/type :pattern-outcome, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :apm-problem, :ref/id "a01A05"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "030fb37f-5e66-4b1d-abe0-e16032a3d414"} {:evidence/body {:event :memory-use, :memory-use {:memory-use/status :pending-outcome, :memory-use/surfaced-ids ["e-0e4e32fe-54af-451b-b302-17aa521891fd" "e-30e87097-f843-4341-81c0-a49ee7ce0ef4" "e-afb1eae8-284f-4551-8c49-d0babd83a780" "e-e7805bcc-6d9f-492d-9bd5-b12d0fbb9dde" "e-ff95cfd3-c645-4b64-afa1-46605015bb00"], :memory-use/domain :mathematics, :memory-use/